{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara","id":1402926,"title":"How powerful and well-protected is Ragara?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-15T03:15:52-07:00","id":1402926,"title":"How powerful and well-protected is Ragara?","content":"He should be immensely powerful even in standard of the Empress' Children to survive while massacring his own sibling; there must have been vendetta and retaliation to extract blood price. From early on, he has cultivated many, many formidable enemies in the Dynasty who will stop at nothing to claim his life, including Mnemon herself. <br /> Besides, why the Empress didn't eliminate Ragara despite of his obvious ambition and killing spree? When Sesus was born, Ragara was already well in his middle age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 07-15-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T05:18:44-07:00","id":1402932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara#post1402926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He should be immensely powerful even in standard of the Empress' Children to survive while massacring his own sibling</div> </div> </div> </div>He would have been rather powerful sure, having risen on a particularly prestigious feat of service and starting off with the advantages of being granted the property of the House whose downfall he enabled. Nevertheless, The Realm refers to his activities of eliminating siblings as having been done quietly. It might also be seen as having occurred during a relatively short period of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there must have been vendetta and retaliation to extract blood price. From early on, he has cultivated many, many formidable enemies in the Dynasty</div> </div> </div> </div>I would feel as though part of the functions of the Scarlet Empress are to stop things from going too far and then forcing Houses to play nice afterwards rather than nursing grudges indefinitely. But I also question this premise; if a person was eliminated by Ragara then it seems to have meant that they <i>didn't</i> have any power yet, that he was doing so before they accumulated such. Tepet and Cathak were not his siblings. Peleps was, but if she was even still alive by then she'd be much more powerful than himself. Houses Mnemon, Sesus, Cynis, Ledaal and V'neef were all founded after his assassination campaign was put to a stop. Mnemon is the only one who survived to have an enduring grudge against him. If Ragara killed you, you weren't leaving behind anybody to carry on such a vendetta, and I kind of think the other Houses weren't too put out if somebody else was doing the work of eliminating imperial scions before they could be endowed as new rivals.<br /> <br /> Let me think some more about the timeline... Nellens died the same year that Sesus was born, so Ragara's ambitions did not outlive him. Nellens was a consort for thirty five years, and House Jurul fell 63 years after he died... but Mnemon was born four years after Nellens became consort...<br /> <br /> Okay, never mind that. I'll just presume that Jurul came up in a period where Ragara had not yet gotten around to killing her, but only got her House after Sesus was born, and then squandered it relatively quickly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">who will stop at nothing to claim his life, including Mnemon herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the order of her intimacies, Mnemon will stop at anything to do with her devotion to the Immaculate Philosophy, ambition to become Empress or pride in her House. Even without those, as a Major Tie she's intrinsically expected to stop at anything that would carry a severe risk to her life or the ruin of what she possesses.<br /> <br /> Ragara and her House look very much as though they're something that would cost everything to destroy if one had no patience about it, and Mnemon's character is not the type to throw everything away in pursuit of such a grudge. I should think Mnemon wants to be in a position of absolute security and power before she deals the final blow, and until that time she'll find needing to co-exist with that enemy outrageous but tolerable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, why the Empress didn't eliminate Ragara despite of his obvious ambition and killing spree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably because there was a window in which it was a lot less obvious. I might also suppose that as a time when the power of the Empress was not quite high enough to deal with him.<br /> <br /> Besides, the whole game of making him responsible for Sesus' protection and only threatening execution if she died (by his hand or otherwise) implies that his elimination was not the first priority, even if I would say she'd have gone through with it if necessary. I'm actually picturing the moment in which Ragara was informed of that decree as one in which she put a lot of power behind it, the kind of thing that effectively cowed him, made him not only believe that she would really do it but could do so without difficulty or hesitation, and left him departing from court nursing bitterness that he had overextended himself to be placed within her power like that, the humiliation of having had his ambitions turned into a sword of Damocles over him, and probably some witnesses to his defeat.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining that Ragara had the kind of power where, on several counts, it would work far more for the Empress to be able to get him to desist in a manner besides killing him. That manner has been working for more than three hundred and fifty years, and I can imagine that for those well acquainted with the history it effectively reinforces the mystique of the Empress.<br /> <br /> Really, given her general tendency to play elaborate mind games with the Great Houses, one might expect the first impulse of the Empress to such underhanded manoeuvring to have been laying the groundwork for putting him in a very dramatic dilemma under her thumb. In the meantime one of Ragara's targets managed to endure impressively enough that she got somebody suited for the founding of another Great House out of it, and one tailor made for further curtailing of Ragara's power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Sesus was born, Ragara was already well in his middle age.</div> </div> </div> </div>One might expect that Ragara spent some time actually building up the power of his House and becoming aware of the fact that the Empress made no distinction between children born to husbands or consorts before he felt comfortable trying to eliminate the competition. I don't really read the thing as having gone on for two hundred years (unless it was <i>very</i> discrete before the final years).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T05:41:08-07:00","id":1402935,"title":"","content":"As a small niggle, Rulinsei also survived Ragara's attentions. And Cynis is likely to have been alive during Ragara's killing years.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Ragara is an old and powerful Exalt. His stats are/will be in Heirs to the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Empress would want to kill her own child, as a mother. Nor would she want to kill one of her most capable and formidable lieutenants, as an Empress. Certainly she was happy to threaten Ragara with death once his ambitions outstripped her use of them.<br /> <br /> I'd say he's pretty well protected and hard to kill. But not meaningfully more so than, say, Mnemon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-15-2020, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:34:08-07:00","id":1402953,"title":"","content":"Ragara's personal security detail would have diminished somewhat since he stepped down as House Matriarch/Patriarch, but you don't make as many enemies as Ragara did and live well past your 300s if you're not a damn good survivor. Ragara's likely got plenty of tricks up his sleeve in case assassins come for him, and he's holed up in Pneuma, which has monks crawling all over it who would take umbrage at someone killing Ragara in <i>their</i> city.<br /> <br /> And politically, killing Ragara doesn't net you much other than the hatred of House Ragara. He's a retired, an old dragon who's lost most of his teeth, most of the political and economic power rests with Ragara Banoba and his inner circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T08:48:55-07:00","id":1402956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1402953#post1402953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ragara's personal security detail would have diminished somewhat since he stepped down as House Matriarch/Patriarch, but you don't make as many enemies as Ragara did and live well past your 300s if you're not a damn good survivor. Ragara's likely got plenty of tricks up his sleeve in case assassins come for him, and he's holed up in Pneuma, which has monks crawling all over it who would take umbrage at someone killing Ragara in <i>their</i> city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that House Iselsi already have one of their members prepeared to assassinate him, and they probably don't want him to get killed by someone else before they decide it would be the right time to kill him.<br /> <br /> That actually makes me wonder if Moonless River was assigned to &quot;watch&quot; Ragara before or after the Empress has vanished- if it was after, then it is probably just a part of House Iselsi carrying the Vendetta. If before... that may have some implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T14:55:05-07:00","id":1402988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1402932#post1402932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nevertheless, The Realm refers to his activities of eliminating siblings as having been done quietly. It might also be seen as having occurred during a relatively short period of time.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> One might expect that Ragara spent some time actually building up the power of his House and becoming aware of the fact that the Empress made no distinction between children born to husbands or consorts before he felt comfortable trying to eliminate the competition. I don't really read the thing as having gone on for two hundred years (unless it was <i>very</i> discrete before the final years).</div> </div> </div> </div>The write-up in Heirs, while obviously still subject to change, confirms your thinking:<br /> <br /> <i>For two centuries, Ragara held the Empress\u2019 personal favor. But that wasn\u2019t enough. He wanted the throne, and for all her affection, the Empress refused to name him as her heir. So he sought to force her hand with a variety of schemes, from elaborate political machinations to unearthing forbidden relics from the First Age. Forestalled in all nonviolent approaches, he ultimately escalated to a <u><b>brief </b></u>but terrifying assassination spree against rival siblings and ministers, with the aim that no other suitable heir would remain.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> As mentioned by JohnDoe above, Ragara's a powerful Exalt in Heirs, at or above the Cainan/Berit end of the scale (albeit we've had it confirmed that his stats as given aren't 100 percent right and need tweaking) even in his dotage (that surprised me, I pretty much had him wheelchair-bound and angry about it in my head canon). On top of that, given who he is and that money is no object, isn't it reasonable to think he's going to be as well-protected as any DB short of Big Red herself can be? We're explicitly told he's waited on by his grandchildren and great-grandchildren plus potentially hearthmates.<br /> <br /> Killing him, a former favourite/heir apparent, while the Empress is around risks her wrath. Killing him \u2013 the founder/figurehead of one of the richest and most influential Great Houses \u2013 in her absence might risk triggering the civil war \u2013 probably something only to be considered once all your ducks are in a row if you are, say, Mnemon or Moonless River.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 07-15-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T07:44:25-07:00","id":1403228,"title":"","content":"Must admit i very much enjoyed Heirs' portrayal of Ragara as someone caught in a threshild between sincerely becoming a more compassionate and overall moral person or surrendering to the ruthless ambition of the past in the present disorder brewing from the power vacuum of the Empress' absence.<br /> <br /> I'm also strongly tempted to tinker a bit with the idea of relatives of some of the top tier houseless exalts like Berith, Amon Mora, Cevis Gandarva and others.<br /> <br /> Also, pardon the ignorance, but who is Moonless River?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T08:16:56-07:00","id":1403233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403228#post1403228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must admit i very much enjoyed Heirs' portrayal of Ragara as someone caught in a threshild between sincerely becoming a more compassionate and overall moral person or surrendering to the ruthless ambition of the past in the present disorder brewing from the power vacuum of the Empress' absence.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also, pardon the ignorance, but who is Moonless River?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard agree!<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Moonless River is an Iselsi sleeper, she's on page 76 of WFHW:<br /> <br /> <i>Moonless River is an Immaculate monk stationed in Pneuma, with a decades-long history of advising those who hope to emulate Pasiap as she does. She\u2019s gained such renown that she receives regular invitations to dine with Ragara himself, and the two have built an amicable relationship. She truly loves the Immaculate lifestyle, and feels personally elevated on a spiritual level by the practice. When she drives her stone-hard fingers through Ragara\u2019s skull on her house\u2019s orders, it won\u2019t be in the name of hate, but of ridding the Realm of the greed that hangs about its neck like a millstone.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 07-17-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T09:17:19-07:00","id":1403241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403233#post1403233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard agree!<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Moonless River is an Iselsi sleeper, she's on page 76 of WFHW:<br /> <br /> <i>Moonless River is an Immaculate monk stationed in Pneuma, with a decades-long history of advising those who hope to emulate Pasiap as she does. She\u2019s gained such renown that she receives regular invitations to dine with Ragara himself, and the two have built an amicable relationship. She truly loves the Immaculate lifestyle, and feels personally elevated on a spiritual level by the practice. When she drives her stone-hard fingers through Ragara\u2019s skull on her house\u2019s orders, it won\u2019t be in the name of hate, but of ridding the Realm of the greed that hangs about its neck like a millstone.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice. And tragically ironic, if one takes in account Ragara's portrayal as sincere but divided in Heirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T03:00:47-07:00","id":1403359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1402935#post1402935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the Empress would want to kill her own child, as a mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see this Edition's characterisation of the Scarlet Empress as particularly less ruthless than prior ones, and in those she has little to nothing of that kind of sentimentality.<br /> <br /> There manage to frequently be mothers willing and capable of killing their own children even without the motivating factors of the secure governance of an empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T05:02:37-07:00","id":1403370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403359#post1403359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see this Edition's characterisation of the Scarlet Empress as particularly less ruthless than prior ones, and in those she has little to nothing of that kind of sentimentality.<br /> <br /> There manage to frequently be mothers willing and capable of killing their own children even without the motivating factors of the secure governance of an empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between being ruthless and being a psychopath.<br /> <br /> Would the Empress kill her children if she had to? Of course. If she had to.<br /> <br /> But she's not killing them because she's bored one Saturday night.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> She allowed Berit to storm off, Mnemon to steal the Thurible, and Ragara to live. Her first response to most problems isn't to bellow &quot;off with their head&quot;. Much of the Empress's success comes from making allies of enemies. Perhaps she doesn't show her children any particular leniency, certainly the Realm favours a certain distance in child rearing. But, in canon, her <i>first</i> response to a problem has never been &quot;murder one of my kids&quot;. Though, certainly, she's not above sacrificing a child if it's necessary. Her solution with Ragara <i>worked</i> -- I don't believe it would have worked if he didn't believe his mother could kill him. If it hadn't worked, I'm sure she would have killed him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-18-2020, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T06:50:26-07:00","id":1403380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403370#post1403370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between being ruthless and being a psychopath.<br /> <br /> Would the Empress kill her children if she had to? Of course. If she had to.<br /> <br /> But she's not killing them because she's bored one Saturday night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is discussing whether she would kill one of her children who is in the process of murdering all of her other children.<br /> Given he's doing this for the sake of inheritance and she's unaging, she might be worried that it will end with her being murdered too.<br /> That's a fairly compelling reason to have someone killed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T09:14:01-07:00","id":1403395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403380#post1403380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is discussing whether she would kill one of her children who is in the process of murdering all of her other children.<br /> Given he's doing this for the sake of inheritance and she's unaging, she might be worried that it will end with her being murdered too.<br /> That's a fairly compelling reason to have someone killed</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So she threatened to kill him and he stopped his killing spree. If he hadn't stopped, she would have killed him.<br /> <br /> But she didn't jump straight to &quot;whelp better kill my son&quot;. She found a solution that kept Ragara alive.<br /> <br /> Perhaps for purely practical reasons. But if a mother chooses not to assassinate her child, I'd like to see positive evidence that maternal feeling plays no roll whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T02:19:18-07:00","id":1403634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403370#post1403370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But she's not killing them because she's bored one Saturday night.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Nobody has ever proposed otherwise.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mind, some portrayals of the Empress do seem to present her as occasionally amusing herself by embroiling promising Dynasts in games with dangerous stakes. The backstory of Ragara Banoba was one such instance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402926-how-powerful-and-well-protected-is-ragara?p=1403395#post1403395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if a mother chooses not to assassinate her child, I'd like to see positive evidence that maternal feeling plays no roll whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that runs into the usual issues of proving a negative.<br /> <br /> I don't know, perhaps if there was ever an instance in which somebody in a similar position to Ragara that was not a child was treated in a more harsh manner.<br /> <br /> (This Edition has not attached the Emerald Thurible to Mnemon in a manner that suggests foul play on her part)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}